  "id": "Compound::DB00734 - Gene::147",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence from the hetionet dataset suggests a potential relationship between Risperidone and Adra1b, mediated through Paliperidone. All three paths indicate that Risperidone causes a variety of effects, including Risus Sardonicus, Eye Rolling, and Pleurothotonus, which are all linked to Paliperidone. Paliperidone, in turn, binds to Adra1b, suggesting a possible mechanism by which Risperidone may influence Adra1b. The shared lowest common ancestors—Risperidone and Paliperidone—point to a common pathway involving the Agent Affecting Nervous System and 1,2-Benzoxazoles, which are structural features of the compounds involved. These findings collectively support a role for Risperidone in modulating Adra1b through its interaction with Paliperidone, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The evidence is consistent across multiple paths, reinforcing the likelihood of a functional relationship between Risperidone and Adra1b.",
